      "text": "I've marked the run as anomalous and put it down to a likely seal leak.\n\n- **What I saw:** Exhaust O2 has risen steadily during growth, from about 3 ppm at 2640 s to 32 ppm at 3120 s, after sitting near 5 ppm through purge and ramp. Normal-run reference values weren't included in this batch, so I can't say how far outside normal that is.\n- **Why a seal leak:** Argon flow is steady at about 100 sccm, so the flow controller isn't stuck. Pressure is steady at about 760 Torr, which argues against a blocked exhaust. Temperature is holding at 750 °C with normal heater power.\n- **Not yet ruled out:** The O2 sensor could be drifting, or oxygen could be coming off the sample or tube.\n- **Suggested next step:** A leak check, such as holding pressure or sniffing the tube seals with helium. My suggestion is recorded only; the run keeps going regardless.\n\nThere's no characterisation data yet. If O2 keeps rising, whatever grows probably won't count as evidence about the recipe."
